single("m2-29", D4, "Your code extracts order details from support emails by using structured outputs in strict mode. The gift_message field appears in only some emails, and requests fail schema validation when you remove it from the required list. You need the field to be optional while strict mode stays on. What should you do?",
 ["Keep it in required and make its type string or null","Turn off strict mode and switch to JSON mode","Remove it from required and allow additional properties","Ask for gift_message in a second request when present"], 1,
 "JSON mode returns valid JSON, but not necessarily your schema, and the code relies on the schema.",
 T("That optional means leaving a field out of required. In strict mode every property is required, so optional means nullable.",
   [["Field sometimes absent, strict mode","Schema","Nullable type, still required"],["Valid JSON, any shape","JSON mode","No schema guarantee"],["Extra keys","additionalProperties","Must be false in strict mode"]],
   [["\"requests fail ... when you remove it from the required list\"","Strict mode needs every property in required."],["\"while strict mode stays on\"","Rules out JSON mode."]],
   "Strict mode: all properties required, additionalProperties false; optional = [\"string\", \"null\"].",
   "Implement solutions to extract entities, topics, summaries, and structured JSON outputs by using generative prompting and Foundry Tools."),
 "Every box on the form stays; you can write 'none' in it.", L+"openai/how-to/structured-outputs"),
